NAVIGATION NOTE (covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass)
  The web /mileage route has no pre-existing AppRoute counterpart (unlike /statistics which aliases to the
  existing .analytics). The four sibling analytics pages each reused an existing AppRoute case; Mileage is a
  genuinely new standalone web route ("Mileage Log" in the web sidebar, web App.tsx L402), so a new .mileage
  case is the honest, minimal way to give it a real navigation home + deep link THROUGH the shared
  infrastructure (not around it). Blast-radius verified:
    - Only AppRoute.swift switches exhaustively over AppRoute (systemImage + group) — both updated.
    - pathSegment falls through to rawValue ("mileage"); AppRouteParser resolves /mileage with no alias needed.
    - MenuCommandCatalog.commands(.navigate) + SpotlightIndexer.indexableRoutes derive from AppRoute.allCases,
      so testNavigateCommandsCoverEveryRoute stays green automatically; testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment +
      testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup also stay green (unique segment, group .insights).
  TeslaSyncApp composes MileageRouteRegistration.registry(.mileage) into the existing chain; no sibling
  registration, the parser, or any other AppRoute case is displaced.

NAME-COLLISION FINDING + FIX (covenant #1 — reported, not masked)
  The first full xcodebuild surfaced 42 errors, 100% rooted in ONE regression I introduced: my public type
  `MileageVehicle` collided with a PRE-EXISTING `public struct MileageVehicle` in the dashboard widget
  TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/MonthlyMileageWidget.Models.swift (1 "ambiguous for type lookup" root error in
  MonthlyMileageWidget.Model.swift + 41 cascading "cannot infer contextual base" in its Previews). FIX: renamed
  my type `MileageVehicle` -> `MileagePageVehicle` across MileageModels/PageModel/Sample + the test + harness
  (the widget owns the `Mileage*` DTO namespace there; my other type names were grep-verified collision-free
  repo-wide). Re-build: the 42 widget errors -> 0 (the widget is byte-unchanged and compiles again).

